&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lincoln Property Company does not accept unsolicited resumes from third-party recruiters unless they were contractually engaged by Lincoln Property Company to provide candidates for a specified opening. Any such employment agency, person or entity that submits an unsolicited resume does so with the acknowledgement and agreement that Lincoln Property Company will have the right to hire that applicant at its discretion without any fee owed to the submitting employment agency, person or entity. At this time, we are not working with any agencies.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Maintenance Technician ensures the integrity of building systems by performing routine maintenance and minor repairs while supporting the efficient operation of equipment. This role provides hands-on support for general maintenance tasks under the supervision of the Chief Engineer or Assistant Chief Engineer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform repairs on toilet facilities, including soap dispensers; clear drains using plungers and handheld augers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct general labor tasks such as carrying, stacking, and sorting materials, and debris removal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and/or replace door hardware, perform minor furniture repairs, and conduct floor maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct basic painting tasks in equipment rooms and perform general cleaning in mechanical spaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replace lamps, air filters, ceiling tiles, and fire extinguishers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform maintenance tasks as assigned; conduct cleaning and inspections of engineering areas and equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use employer-provided vehicles to travel for parts and supplies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow company safety protocols and use PPE for all tasks; ensure compliance with OSHA, NEC, NFC, and NFPA regulations; report hazards immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call rotations and respond to emergencies; handle urgent tenant service requests and support recovery efforts during severe weather and system outages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact with tenants, contractors, and property managers while carrying out maintenance tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work under the direction of senior engineers and supervisors to develop skills in maintenance and repairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High School Diploma/GED or 1-2 years of job-related experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering and trade licenses required per local, state, or national requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CFC Certification preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing proficiency in basic hand tool operation and mechanical repairs; gaining exposure to HVAC, plumbing, and electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic skills with Microsoft Office Outlook and laptop/phone applications for work order systems, email, and training platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand, walk, climb ladders, and lift up to 50 pounds; ability to perform physically demanding tasks such as stooping, crouching, and kneeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States without the need for visa sponsorship now or in the future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to stand, walk, climb ladders, and lift up to 50 pounds. Must be able to perform physically demanding tasks such as stooping, crouching, and kneeling.&lt;/p&gt;
